  <exercise number="223" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>$$\underset{x\rightarrow 0}{\text{lim}}x^{2}\text{cos}\mspace{2mu}\left( {2\pi x} \right) = 0$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>Since $$-1 \leq \text{cos}(2\pi x) \leq 1,$$ then $$- x^{2} \leq x^{2}\text{cos}(2\pi x) \leq x^{2}.$$ Since $$\underset{x\rightarrow 0}{\text{lim}}x^{2} = 0 = \underset{x\rightarrow 0}{\text{lim}} - x^{2},$$ it follows that $$\underset{x\rightarrow 0}{\text{lim}}x^{2}\text{cos}\mspace{2mu}\left( {2\pi x} \right) = 0.$$</p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
